## 2. Longform — quality upgrade (after it connects again)

- [ ] **Make longform load the real persona `.md` system prompts.** Currently `fetchEpisode()` reconstructs a thin prompt from the persona *name only* (`You are ${name}...`) and never reads the authored `.md`. Result: longform ignores all the persona work and leans on the model's generic knowledge. Change: read the persona's identity prompt, prepend it to the essay-format instructions.
  - Payoff: the modernised prompts then drive all three outputs, not just Judgement + chatbot.

## 3. Persona roster — reconcile the three-way mismatch

- [ ] **The three files disagree on who exists.** `run-judgements.js` knows 18 personas; `run-longform.cjs` knows 27; `run-longform.bat` help text lists 28. Membership conflicts too (e.g. `marx` is in longform but not judgements; judgements uses id `adamsmith`, longform uses `smith`).
  - Pick one canonical roster (likely `personas.json` or a shared module), have all runners read from it, so a persona can't silently exist in one mode and not another.

